 "summary": "Develops a cross regional small business partnership program.",
 "title": "Develops a cross regional small business partnership program",
 "vetoMessages": {
  "items": [
   {
    "billId": {
     "basePrintNo": "A8308",
     "basePrintNoStr": "A8308-2013",
     "printNo": "A8308",
     "session": 2013,
     "version": ""
    },
    "billPage": 0,
    "chapter": 0,
    "lineEnd": 0,
    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": "\n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 541\n\nTO THE ASSEMBLY:\n\nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n\nAssembly Bill Number 8308-B, entitled:\n\n    \"AN ACT to amend the economic development law, in relation to estab-\n      lishing a cross regional small business partnership program\"\n\n    NOT APPROVED\n\n  This  bill  would  require  the  Department of Economic Development to\nestablish a regional small business partnership program to foster  part-\nnerships between small businesses from different regions of the State.\n\n  At  the  recent  Upstate Downstate Summit, I covered specific concerns\nthat this legislation is  intended  to  address.  The  Summit  addressed\nprioritizing the opening of new markets and increasing opportunities for\nNew  York  State agriculture producers. The Summit also addressed how to\nmaximize business between  upstate  producers  and  downstate  consumers\nthrough  the  State's  multi-billion  dollar  agriculture  industry. The\nSummit further addressed the development of a  Regional  Food  Hub  Task\nForce  and  Action Plan aimed at expanding regional food hubs across New\nYork State.\n\n  While this bill is well-intentioned, it comes without funding.  Imple-\nmenting  this  new  program  successfully  would   require   significant\nresources which this bill fails to provide. Proposals such as this which\nrequire  State  expenditures  should  be negotiated during the budgeting\nprocess when all the financial demands of the State are evaluated simul-\ntaneously. Therefore, I am vetoing this bill.\n\n  The bill is disapproved.                    (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n\n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
    "vetoNumber": 541,
    "vetoType": "STANDARD",
    "year": 2014
   }
  ],
  "size": 1
 },
